From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:29:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] [WarpSpecialize] Guard prelude placement, outer-if
 partitions, and loop-carried postludes

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5
Upstream-commit: 438e2db04ff52b263f8ad36ed89e0c878930262a
Upstream-pr: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3869, https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/pull/3883

Rationale: Fix three correctness hazards in ProducerConsumerWarpSpecialized:
1. Keep shared-prelude statements at their original control-flow position instead of hoisting them across sibling statements, and keep producer-free branches guarded to the consumer thread range (#3663 / #3685).
2. When a warp-specialized T.Pipelined loop sits alone inside a thread-invariant IfThenElse whose condition does not read buffers written by the branch, split the producer and consumer partitions outside the if so setmaxnreg instructions execute uniformly at the partition root (#3869, fixes #3664).
3. Decline warp specialization when a T.Pipelined loop inside an outer serial loop has post-pipeline local buffer writes that feed pre-pipeline producer reads on the next outer iteration without an inter-iteration barrier (#3883, fixes #3842).

Quality: Prevents miscompilation of warp-specialized pipelines under outer conditionals and serial loops while keeping all 33 existing spark-ds41f:1107 kernels byte-for-byte unchanged.

Tests: testing/python/transform/test_tilelang_transform_producer_consumer_ws_persistent.py across two GPU boots on SM121.

Upstream-status: Backported from tile-ai/tilelang#3685 (commit 438e2db04ff5), open PR tile-ai/tilelang#3869, and open PR tile-ai/tilelang#3883.
